        <briefdescription>
<para>Token helpers (used by lexer internally and by tests) </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>These functions are used to create and free tokens, check for operators, and read operators and words from the input string. They are also used by the unit tests to verify the correctness of the lexer implementation.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>type</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The type of the token to create. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>value</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The raw string value of the token (with quotes preserved). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>io_number</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The file descriptor number for redirection tokens (set to -1 if not applicable).</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>A new t_list node containing the created token, or NULL on allocation failure. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
